# Keep the build context small — every file under the build context
# is sent to the Docker daemon at build time, so excluding everything
# we don't need cuts build time + image size.

# Build outputs
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo

# Dependencies (re-installed inside the image)
**/node_modules

# Test + dev artefacts
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.jest-cache

# Local env files — secrets must come from the deploy environment,
# never from the build context. Include the example so devs can see
# the expected shape.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!apps/api/.env.example

# IDE / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Git internals — Dockerfile can capture build SHA via build args
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Logs
*.log
**/*.log

# Local dev infrastructure (Postgres data, Mailhog state, etc.)
infra/docker-compose/data

# Repo-level docs not needed in the image
docs
reference
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
SMOKE_TEST.md
SESSION_HANDOFF.md
PRODUCTION_HANDOVER.md

# Web app — not part of the API image
apps/web

# Test files — not shipped to production
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts
**/test
**/__tests__
